==================================================================
DEFECTS FOR THE LEAD (neither is a criterion failure)
==================================================================
D1  TestWarningsKey_OrderInvariant's non-mutation assertion is vacuous: it
    inspects `a := []string{"a","b"}`, which is already sorted, so an in-place
    sort cannot perturb it. Proven green under PROBE D (sorting the caller's
    slice in place). The implementation is correct — I proved non-mutation
    with an unsorted caller-visible slice and end-to-end on pageData.Warnings —
    but the shipped guard would not catch a regression. Fix: assert on the
    permuted slice `b` (["b","a"]) instead of, or as well as, `a`.
    Location: internal/handlers/accounts/handlers_test.go, the block commented
    "warningsKey must sort a COPY for hashing, not the caller's slice".
D2  TestHandlePage_RendererMode_NoOverlapRendersNoWarningBlock scans the whole
    response body for the bare string "Pattern overlap warning", which
    includes the always-rendered <script> block. It therefore constrains
    unrelated script copy, has already forced one wording change, and will
    misfire again. Full reasoning and a scoped replacement under criterion 10.
